Package: shinygazer
Type: Package
Title: Interactive Pupil Pre-Processing with 'gazeR'
Version: 0.3.1
Authors@R: c(
  person("Jason", "Geller", email = "drjasongeller@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: A 'shiny' app for pre-processing pupillometry data without
    writing code, built on the 'gazeR' package. Reads EyeLink .asc files, SR
    Research Data Viewer sample reports, Tobii (Titta) and Pupil Labs Neon
    exports; removes blinks (tracker events or noise-based detection) and
    artifacts; interpolates, smooths, baseline-corrects and time-locks trials;
    reports data quality and behavioural exclusions; and plots time courses
    with within- or between-subject error, rainclouds and pupil-behaviour
    relationships. Every setting is exported so the pipeline can be reproduced.
URL: https://github.com/jgeller112/shiny-gazeR
BugReports: https://github.com/jgeller112/shiny-gazeR/issues
